  "description": "Defines maximum safe light exposure levels for artifacts based on material sensitivity",
  "definition": "High sensitivity artifacts (textiles, paper) must not exceed 50 lux; Medium sensitivity (paintings, wood) must not exceed 200 lux. Based on conservation research about light-induced deterioration rates."
}

